Service probe database for Pulse (`--probe-db`)
===============================================

The base of probes.json is the probe database embedded in GenDec/Pulse,
copied verbatim.

  Source:   https://github.com/onixus/GenDec  (src/scanner/probes.json)
  Tag:      v1.3.0
  Version:  2026.08.21 (the "version" field of the file)
  sha256:   ee2c2c71e9c0c04ecbabdc3abb195f35acfe35477b56834bb451304c4ffa1a1a
  Licence:  MIT (Cargo.toml: license = "MIT", authors = ["GenA"]).
            The upstream repository carries no LICENSE file, so the standard
            MIT text is reproduced below with the author named in Cargo.toml.

Provenance of the base, and what is claimed
-------------------------------------------

What we know about the upstream set comes from two statements in the GenDec
repository at tag v1.3.0, nothing more:

  * src/scanner/probe_db.rs, the comment on EMBEDDED_PROBE_DB: "The shipped
    probe set. Written by hand for Pulse -- the Nmap `nmap-service-probes`
    file is NPSL-licensed and is not used here."
  * Cargo.toml: license = "MIT", authors = ["GenA"]. GenDec has no LICENSE
    file at its root, so the MIT text below is the standard text with the
    copyright holder taken from that field.

We have not independently verified either statement and have no confirmation
from the author beyond them. We therefore claim exactly this: the base is the
upstream set as its author describes it. Do not read it as a clean-room
guarantee made by this project.

Rules added after the upstream entries (see docs/pulse-backend.md, "Probe
database") are written from scratch for this project, from banners observed on
our own test stand and from vendor documentation. They are not derived from
Nmap's nmap-service-probes (NPSL).

